notify-senechal.sh step 2 reports a FALSE FAIL on the fully-successful path. Its check is `ahead > 0` after `scheduler -i senechal`, but -i PUSHES itself whenever the target repo is not behind origin (the script header says so: it only skips the push when behind). So on the happy path there is nothing left to push, ahead == 0, and the guard dies with "nothing to push after scheduler -i -- the note was not committed, and this script will not report success for a write that did not happen" -- immediately after printing "committed + pushed in senechal". Witnessed 2026-07-26 filing the scheduler front-door marker change: the note DID land (senechal 92ebe82, contained in origin/main, .claude/FOCUS.md +2). Fails CLOSED, which is the right direction, but it will cry wolf on every successful notification and train the human to ignore a guard that exists to be believed. Fix: verify CONTAINMENT, not ahead-ness -- capture HEAD after step 1 and assert `git merge-base --is-ancestor $sha @{u}` (plus that the commit touches the expected file), which is true whether -i pushed or this script pushes. Keep the die() for the genuinely-not-committed case: HEAD unchanged by step 1.
